# install from the proxy (typed): virtio-blk and fs give the disk's
# System and data volumes, virtio-net and inet the network. On the host,
# e2e.sh runs tools/api-proxy/e2e_serve.py (serve), whose proxy on
# @PORT@, which agent/config names at 10.0.2.2, serves the case's
# release for virt. install --net fresh System formats System and
# fetches the release onto it and onto data: the system's files, a
# program marked one, the agent's seed and the model, and makes data's
# agent, speech and user directories and the home's other parts. The
# shell then writes the agent's rules anew, and install --net update
# System fetches the system again but keeps the rules, the board's
# token and config, and passes over the model, the same already.
start /bin/sh
start /sbin/uart noecho
start /sbin/virtio-blk
start /sbin/fs
start /sbin/virtio-net
start /sbin/inet
dev /sbin/uart
dev /sbin/virtio-blk
dev /sbin/virtio-net
